## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable, fault-tolerant streaming pipeline with privacy controls for distributed data.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming ingestion with exactly-once guarantees
- Replay protection using nonces and signatures
- Per-region DP budgets and auditability
- Fault tolerance for intermittent connectivity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo idempotent sink
function ingestEvent(event, store) {
  const key = event.device_id + ':' + event.nonce;
  if (store.exists(key)) return;
  store.write(key, event.score);
  // update region aggregates atomically
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test replay protection under clock skew?
- How would you validate exactly-once semantics across partitions?

## Why This Is Asked
Schema evolution is common in production systems. This tests ability to plan backward-compatible changes that don’t break existing clients.

## Key Concepts
- API versioning and data contracts
- Migration scripts and defaulting
- Feature flags and canary rollouts
- Regression and contract tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Migration mapping
function migrate(payload) {
  if (payload.score_source) return payload;
  if (payload.model_version >= 2) payload.score_source = 'model';
  else payload.score_source = 'heuristic';
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
